# GitHub handoff (HARD)

Issue state on GitHub is not proof of completion when work was never pushed. **Maintainers cannot review code that is not on the remote.**

## Mandatory sequence (every Feature-track GitHub issue)

When a **GitHub issue** is finished (tests passed, ready for human review):

```text
1. Pick up issue      → assign yourself; optional `status/in-progress` label
2. Implement + run    → relevant tests from setup.md; capture **actual output**
3. Commit + push      → `development` only; message references issue (`Fixes #n` or `Refs #n`)
4. GitHub comment     → one evidence post (template below) on the issue
5. Labels             → add `status/ready-for-review`; remove `status/in-progress` if used
```

**Order is strict:** never post handoff before commit + push succeed. Never hand off with uncommitted work.

## Who closes issues

- **Agents:** do **not** close Feature issues. Post evidence and `status/ready-for-review`.
- **Maintainers:** close after verifying the handoff (often when work is merged to `main` or accepted on `development`).

Direct-track work may close without ceremony when the human asked for a one-off fix.

## Sprint pickup

When the human says **“pick up sprint X”**:

1. List **all** open issues for that sprint (GitHub **milestone** or `sprint-*` label — see `docs/project/sprints.md`).
2. Complete each issue with the sequence above.
3. **Commit + push + issue comment after each issue** — not one batch at sprint end.

Use **`gh`** for issue/milestone operations when available.

## Required comment (single post)

Post **after** push.

```markdown
## Ready for review — #n (YYYY-MM-DD)

### Acceptance criteria
- [x] <AC verbatim> — <evidence: file/line, endpoint, or UI path>
- [ ] <AC unmet> — <why / what's left>

### How to verify

**Committed code**
- Branch: `development`
- Commit: `<full SHA>` — `<one-line subject>`
- Issue: https://github.com/<org>/<repo>/issues/n

**Tests** (paste output — not “tests green”)
```text
<paste relevant command + exit code + summary lines>
```

**UI / dashboard** (when visual AC applies)
- Local: `make dev` / `make build` + `./bin/dockyard serve` → steps
- OR preview URL / recording when available

### Reviewer verdicts (Feature track, when reviewers ran)
| Subagent | Verdict |
|-|-|
| code-reviewer | PASS / FAIL / N/A |
| … | … |

### Deviations from spec
- **None** or explicit delta

### Reference
- Spec: `docs/project/issues/<n>/spec.md`
- Feedback: `docs/project/feedback/<n>/` (when applicable)
```

## Evidence bar (HARD)

| Required | Insufficient |
|--|--|
| `development` + **full commit SHA** after push | Local-only diff, missing SHA |
| **Pasted test output** | “All pass” with no command |
| AC checkboxes with **verifiable pointers** | Checkmarks without evidence |
| Issue comment **after** push | Claiming done in chat only |

Update `roadmap.md` / `generator-state.md` when a milestone slice lands. Changelog + patch bump per [changelog](changelog.mdc) when the issue cycle closes.

Template copy: `docs/project/templates/github-handoff-comment.md`
